; pi4V3dTex.pi4 - V3D milestone 1: a TMU-SAMPLED TEXTURED triangle.
;
; DIAGNOSTIC. Does not ship.
;
; ======================================================================
;  WHAT THIS PROGRAM CLAIMS, AND WHAT IT REFUSES TO CLAIM
; ======================================================================
;
;  pi4V3dTri.pi4 drew ONE FLAT-COLOURED triangle: the colour came from
;  a per-draw uniform, there were NO varyings and NO texture sampling.
;  This program adds BOTH, which is the hardest part of a V3D driver:
;
;    * a COORDINATE and a VERTEX shader that, on top of the clip-space
;      position pi4V3dTri emits, write U,V out as VARYINGS in the VPM
;      varying segment (coord offset 6/7, vertex offset 4/5 -
;      v3d_nir_lower_io.c:399-433);
;    * a FRAGMENT shader that reads the two interpolated varyings with
;      the LDVARY signal, writes S and T to the TMU, FIRES the sample
;      by writing TMUS, takes the LDTMU signal to read the returned
;      texel and writes it to the TLB;
;    * a TEXTURE_SHADER_STATE record and a SAMPLER_STATE record built
;      by hand from v3d_packet.xml:1493-1532 and :1584-1618 (there is
;      no library helper for either);
;    * a 4x4 RGBA8 checkerboard texture TFU-tiled to a T-format
;      (LINEARTILE) texture the TMU can sample.
;
;  THE PASS CRITERION IS COUNTED PIXELS AND A COLOUR SPLIT, NOT A
;  PICTURE. The 4x4 texture is RED in columns 0,1 and BLUE in columns
;  2,3 - a pure VERTICAL split. The triangle's U coordinate is a linear
;  function of screen X only (u = (x - 8) / 48, see below), so every
;  pixel left of the split samples RED and every pixel right of it
;  samples BLUE. The whole 64x64 buffer is read back on the CPU and:
;
;    * RED and BLUE pixels are counted and their X bounding boxes taken;
;    * the pass demands nRed>0, nBlue>0 AND max-x(RED) < min-x(BLUE),
;      i.e. EVERY red pixel is strictly left of EVERY blue pixel.
;
;  WHY THAT SHAPE. It proves three things at once and depends on NONE
;  of the unknowns pi4V3dTri left open:
;    - two DISTINCT texture colours appear, so the TMU sampled a
;      texture rather than a flat uniform (a flat colour gives one
;      colour and fails nRed>0 AND nBlue>0);
;    - the split is a clean vertical line, so the U varying was
;      INTERPOLATED across X (a constant varying gives one colour; a
;      varying that leaked Y-dependence would put red and blue pixels
;      at overlapping X and fail max-x(RED) < min-x(BLUE));
;    - it is Y-CONVENTION INDEPENDENT. pi4V3dTri could not decide
;      whether the stored row increases or decreases with Ys; here the
;      colour depends on X ALONE, so the verdict does not care. The V
;      varying is emitted and interpolated (both LDVARY paths run) but
;      the texture is V-uniform on purpose, so a wrong V cannot decide
;      the verdict.
;
;  THE COLOURS ARE 0x00/0xFF ONLY, ON PURPOSE. RED is $FF0000FF and
;  BLUE is $FFFF0000 in the framebuffer's byte order (R low, A high -
;  pi4V3dTri proved that order). The texel channels are 0.0 and 1.0,
;  which round-trip f32 -> f16 -> unorm8 EXACTLY, so unlike pi4V3dTri
;  this test has no rounding slop to reason about at all.
;
; ======================================================================
;  THE U,V ARITHMETIC, WHY IT IS AFFINE, AND THE VARYING MODEL
; ======================================================================
;
;  The three vertices carry (in pixels / UV): (8,8)/(0,0),
;  (56,8)/(1,0), (8,56)/(0,1). Solving u = a*x + b*y + c through those
;  three gives b = 0, a = 1/48, c = -8/48 - i.e. u = (x - 8) / 48,
;  INDEPENDENT OF Y. The u=0.5 split lands at x=32, halfway across.
;
;  Wc IS 1.0 FOR ALL THREE VERTICES (as in pi4V3dTri), so 1/Wc = 1 and
;  the varying is AFFINE. For that case perspective and no-perspective
;  interpolation are numerically identical (dividing by w=1 is a
;  no-op), so this program uses the SIMPLER no-perspective shader
;  arithmetic - emit_noperspective_varying(), nir_to_vir.c:1027-1029:
;
;      result = vary_reg + r5
;
;  where the LDVARY signal delivers the interpolation value to the
;  register named in its signal-address field (rf10/rf11 here) and
;  loads the C coefficient into r5 with ONE cycle of delay
;  (qpu_schedule.c:590-592 - r5 may not be read within one tick of an
;  ldvary on 4.2). One filler instruction sits in that delay slot.
;
;  THE FLAGS PACKET MUST AGREE WITH THIS ARITHMETIC, and getting it
;  wrong is what pinned every fragment's U at 0 on the first silicon
;  run. The no-perspective form (vary + r5) requires the varying to be
;  declared NO-PERSPECTIVE in the bin list; leaving the flags ZEROED
;  (perspective) instead makes the hardware deliver the varying for the
;  perspective form (vary * payload_w + r5), and reading that with
;  vary + r5 returns the provoking-vertex value - which looks exactly
;  like flat shading. So this program emits an explicit Non-perspective
;  Flags packet with bits set for varyings 0 and 1 (EmitNonperspFlags).
;  For an affine (Wc=1) quad screen-linear interpolation is the correct
;  interpolation, so the no-perspective path is exact.
;
; ======================================================================
;  THE FRAGMENT SHADER'S TMU SEQUENCE
; ======================================================================
;
;  Config is pushed to the TMU config FIFO with the WRTMUC signal, one
;  uniform per WRTMUC (vir_WRTMUC = a NOP carrying sig.wrtmuc and a
;  uniform, v3d40_tex.c):
;
;    P0 = TEXTURE_SHADER_STATE address | return-words mask.
;         The state is 16-byte aligned so its low 4 bits carry the
;         mask; RGBA at 32-bit output is four words, mask $F
;         (TMU Config Parameter 0, v3d_packet.xml:1435-1438;
;         return_words = (1 << num_components) - 1).
;    P1 = SAMPLER_STATE address | output-type-32-bit(bit0).
;         8-byte aligned; bit0 makes the TMU return four f32 words so
;         the TLB write below is byte-for-byte pi4V3dTri's
;         (TMU Config Parameter 1, :1440-1445).
;
;  Then the coordinates: T to TMUT, S to TMUS. Writing TMUS FIRES the
;  lookup (it is the trigger register for a sampler read). Four LDTMU
;  signals read the four f32 channels R,G,B,A into rf0..rf3; the thread
;  stalls on the first LDTMU until the TMU delivers. Finally, after the
;  last THRSW, two VFPACKs pack (R,G) and (B,A) into 2xf16 and write
;  TLBU then TLB - IDENTICAL to pi4V3dTri's colour write, only the
;  source is the sampled texel instead of a uniform.
;
; ======================================================================
;  UNPROVEN / GUESSED, FOR THE BENCH TO WATCH (also in the report)
; ======================================================================
;   * The TEXTURE_SHADER_STATE and SAMPLER_STATE BIT PACKING is built
;     by hand from the packet layout - there is no encoder for it in
;     v3d.pi4 and no offline oracle. If a swizzle, a dimension or the
;     texture-type code is off, the texel is wrong or the TMU faults.
;   * The LDVARY -> r5 one-cycle delay is from Mesa's SCHEDULER, not
;     from any 4.2 doc, and v3dqpu.pi4's hazard checker does NOT police
;     it. If the real latency is larger the varyings are garbage.
;   * P2 (TMU Config Parameter 2) is NOT written - Mesa omits it for a
;     plain nearest 2D sample. If this silicon needs it, the lookup
;     misconfigures.
;   * TMUS as the trigger and the T-before-S write order.
;   * return-words = $F giving exactly four LDTMU words.
;
; ======================================================================
;  MEMORY MAP - identity-mapped through the V3D MMU, VA = PA. The
;  guard page at $65C000 is DELIBERATELY NOT MAPPED and sits right
;  after the 16 KiB target.
; ======================================================================
;
; BUILT WITH --entry-returns, so it returns to a resident monitor and a
; wrong answer costs a line of output rather than a power cycle:
;
;   PureMetalForge.exe --compile RaspberryPi4/Examples/Diagnostics/pi4V3dTex.pi4 -t pi4 \
;       --load-addr 0x400000 --stack-addr 0x3000000 --entry-returns \
;       -o RaspberryPi4/Examples/Diagnostics/pi4V3dTex.img
;
; The load/bss/stack match pi4V3dTri.pi4 (its own build line uses
; --load-addr 0x400000 --stack-addr 0x3000000). Flash and run: send the
; payload to $400000 with the monitor's `b <addr> <len> <crc>` then
; `go 0x400000`. Arm the deadman first: this starts the TFU and the
; graphics pipeline, both bus masters behind their own page table.
; ======================================================================

XIncludeFile "RaspberryPi4/Lib/mailbox.pi4"
XIncludeFile "RaspberryPi4/Lib/v3d.pi4"
XIncludeFile "RaspberryPi4/Lib/v3dqpu.pi4"

#UART_DR = $FE201000
#UART_FR = $FE201018

; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
;  THE MEMORY MAP. Same base layout as pi4V3dTri, with the encoder
;  corpus dropped and three texture pages put in its place.
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
#TEX_PT        = $640000
#TEX_PT_BYTES  = 16384
#TEX_ILLEGAL   = $648000
#TEX_BCL       = $650000
#TEX_TILELIST  = $651000
#TEX_RCL       = $652000
#TEX_TSTATE    = $653000
; The shader state record plus its ten attribute records.
#TEX_SHREC     = $654000
; The vertex data, and the default attribute values 256 bytes in.
#TEX_VERTS     = $655000
#TEX_DEFAULTS  = $655100
; The three uniform streams, 64 bytes apart in one page.
#TEX_UNIF_CS   = $656000
#TEX_UNIF_VS   = $656040
#TEX_UNIF_FS   = $656080
; The three QPU programs, 512 bytes apart in one page.
#TEX_CODE_CS   = $657000
#TEX_CODE_VS   = $657200
#TEX_CODE_FS   = $657400
#TEX_CODE_SLOT = 512
#TEX_TARGET    = $658000
#TEX_GUARD     = $65C000
; The texture pages. TEXSRC is the raster checkerboard the TFU reads;
; TEX is the LINEARTILE texture the TFU writes and the TMU samples;
; TEXSTATE holds the texture shader state at +0 and the sampler state
; at +256 (both well inside one page, both aligned enough).
#TEX_TEXSRC    = $65D000
#TEX_TEX       = $65E000
#TEX_TEXSTATE  = $65F000
#TEX_SAMPSTATE = $65F100
#TEX_TALLOC    = $660000
#TEX_OVERFLOW  = $700000

#TEX_PAGE          = 4096
#TEX_BCL_BYTES     = 4096
#TEX_TL_BYTES      = 4096
#TEX_RCL_BYTES     = 4096
#TEX_TSTATE_BYTES  = 4096
#TEX_SHREC_BYTES   = 4096
#TEX_VERTS_BYTES   = 4096
#TEX_UNIF_BYTES    = 4096
#TEX_CODE_BYTES    = 4096
#TEX_TARGET_BYTES  = 16384
#TEX_GUARD_BYTES   = 4096
#TEX_TEX_BYTES     = 4096
#TEX_TALLOC_BYTES  = $84000
#TEX_OVERFLOW_BYTES = 262144

#TEX_W      = 64
#TEX_H      = 64
#TEX_STRIDE = 256
#TEX_PIXELS = 4096

; The 4x4 texture: RGBA8, columns 0,1 red, columns 2,3 blue. Word order
; is R low / A high, the order pi4V3dTri's clear proved.
#TEX_TW     = 4
#TEX_TH     = 4
#TEX_TBYTES = 64                ; 4*4*4
#TEX_RED    = $FF0000FF         ; R=FF G=00 B=00 A=FF
#TEX_BLUE   = $FFFF0000         ; R=00 G=00 B=FF A=FF

#TEX_CLEAR  = $44332211
#TEX_POISON = $A5A5A5A5

; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
;  THE FRAGMENT-SHADER MODE. Three builds from one source.
;
;  #TEX_FS_MODE = 0  TEXTURED: read the two varyings, sample the TMU,
;                    write the texel. The M1 goal.
;  #TEX_FS_MODE = 1  SOLID: read and DISCARD both varyings, no TMU, write
;                    a solid colour from four uniforms - pi4V3dTri's flat
;                    shader shape. Isolates the TMU path from the render
;                    CL and the varying path.
;  #TEX_FS_MODE = 2  URAMP: read varying 0 (U) and write it to ALL FOUR
;                    colour channels as a grayscale. NO TMU. This makes
;                    the interpolated U value directly VISIBLE and
;                    READABLE per pixel: framebuffer byte = round(U*255).
;                    If U interpolates, the triangle is a left-to-right
;                    gradient; if it is constant (the current bug), the
;                    triangle is one flat grey and its level tells us the
;                    exact stuck U value. This isolates the varying read
;                    from the texture entirely.
;
;  In ALL THREE the coordinate and vertex shaders (which emit the
;  varyings), the shader record (numVaryingsFs = 2), the VPM sizing and
;  the render CL are identical - only the fragment shader and its uniform
;  stream change.
;
;  Build: edit #TEX_FS_MODE, recompile. 0 -> pi4V3dTex.img,
;  1 -> pi4V3dTexSolid.img, 2 -> pi4V3dTexRamp.img. All load at 0x400000,
;  run with `go 0x400000`.
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
#TEX_FS_MODE = 0

#TEX_MODE_TEX    = 0
#TEX_MODE_SOLID  = 1
#TEX_MODE_RAMP   = 2
; DIRECT: the U-ramp fragment shader, but the coordinate and vertex
; shaders source varying0 = Xc and varying1 = Yc (the clip position,
; a known-good per-vertex float) INSTEAD of the U,V attributes. This
; bypasses the attribute->VPM plumbing: if this ramp shows a gradient,
; the interpolator works and the bug is U-attribute-specific; if it is
; still flat, the interpolation setup itself is broken.
#TEX_MODE_DIRECT = 3

; The solid colour for the bisection build: GREEN, $FF00FF00 in the
; framebuffer's byte order (R=00 G=FF B=00 A=FF). Distinct from red,
; blue, clear and poison. Channels are 0.0 and 1.0, exact through f16.
#TEX_SOLID  = $FF00FF00
#TEX_SF_R   = $00000000         ; 0.0
#TEX_SF_G   = $3F800000         ; 1.0
#TEX_SF_B   = $00000000         ; 0.0
#TEX_SF_A   = $3F800000         ; 1.0

#TEX_ZCLEAR = $3F800000

#TEX_F_ZERO   = $00000000
#TEX_F_ONE    = $3F800000
#TEX_F_P75    = $3F400000
#TEX_F_M75    = $BF400000
#TEX_F_8192   = $46000000

; The TLB configuration word the fragment shader's TLBU write pulls
; from the uniform stream. $FFFFFFFF = normal vec4 f16 RT0, the same
; value and the same reasoning as pi4V3dTri.
#TEX_TLB_CONF = $FFFFFFFF

; The three vertices, in PIXELS, and the viewport centre.
#TEX_V0X = 8
#TEX_V0Y = 8
#TEX_V1X = 56
#TEX_V1Y = 8
#TEX_V2X = 8
#TEX_V2Y = 56
#TEX_CX  = 32
#TEX_CY  = 32

#TEX_WAIT_US = 100000

; ======================================================================
;  PRINTING - lifted unchanged from pi4V3dTri.
; ======================================================================

Procedure PutC(c.i)
  Define f.i
  Repeat
    f = PeekN(#UART_FR)
  Until (f & 32) = 0
  PokeL(#UART_DR, c)
EndProcedure

Procedure PutS(*s)
  Define i.i
  Define c.i
  i = 0
  Repeat
    c = PeekA(*s + i)
    If c = 0 : Break : EndIf
    PutC(c)
    i = i + 1
  ForEver
EndProcedure

Procedure PutNl()
  PutC(13) : PutC(10)
EndProcedure

Procedure PutHex(v.i, digits.i)
  Define i.i
  Define n.i
  For i = digits - 1 To 0 Step -1
    n = (v >> (i * 4)) & $F
    If n < 10
      PutC(48 + n)
    Else
      PutC(55 + n)
    EndIf
  Next
EndProcedure

Procedure PutDec(v.i)
  Define d.i
  Define started.i
  Define digit.i
  If v < 0
    PutC(45)
    v = 0 - v
  EndIf
  If v = 0
    PutC(48)
    ProcedureReturn
  EndIf
  d = 1000000000000000000
  started = 0
  While d > 0
    digit = (v / d) % 10
    If digit <> 0 Or started = 1
      PutC(48 + digit)
      started = 1
    EndIf
    d = d / 10
  Wend
EndProcedure

Procedure PutPad(*name, width.i)
  Define i.i
  Define c.i
  i = 0
  Repeat
    c = PeekA(*name + i)
    If c = 0 : Break : EndIf
    PutC(c)
    i = i + 1
  ForEver
  While i < width
    PutC(32)
    i = i + 1
  Wend
EndProcedure

Procedure RowHex(*name, v.i)
  PutS("  ")
  PutPad(*name, 28)
  PutS("$")
  PutHex(v, 8)
  PutNl()
EndProcedure

Procedure RowDec(*name, v.i)
  PutS("  ")
  PutPad(*name, 28)
  PutDec(v)
  PutNl()
EndProcedure

Procedure PutErr(e.i)
  Select e
    Case #V3D_OK
      PutS("OK")
    Case #V3D_ERR_NOINIT
      PutS("NOINIT - V3dInit() has not passed")
    Case #V3D_ERR_MMU_OFF
      PutS("MMU_OFF - no V3D page table")
    Case #V3D_ERR_MMU_FAULT
      PutS("MMU_FAULT - a page walk failed. See VIO_ADDR.")
    Case #V3D_ERR_MMU_ALIGN
      PutS("MMU_ALIGN - an address is not aligned enough")
    Case #V3D_ERR_MMU_RANGE
      PutS("MMU_RANGE - outside the page table, or page 0")
    Case #V3D_ERR_MMU_FLUSH
      PutS("MMU_FLUSH - the TLB clear never finished")
    Case #V3D_ERR_CACHE_TIMEOUT
      PutS("CACHE_TIMEOUT - the L2T clean never finished")
    Case #V3D_ERR_CL_ARGS
      PutS("CL_ARGS - a field or a buffer will not do")
    Case #V3D_ERR_CL_FULL
      PutS("CL_FULL - the list ran out of room")
    Case #V3D_ERR_CL_NOBUF
      PutS("CL_NOBUF - a packet with no list open")
    Case #V3D_ERR_BIN_TIMEOUT
      PutS("BIN_TIMEOUT - CLE_BFC never moved")
    Case #V3D_ERR_BIN_OOM
      PutS("BIN_OOM - the tile allocation pool ran out")
    Case #V3D_ERR_RENDER_TIMEOUT
      PutS("RENDER_TIMEOUT - CLE_RFC never moved")
    Case #V3D_ERR_JOB_BUSY
      PutS("JOB_BUSY - the render was offered before the bin finished")
    Case #V3D_ERR_TFU_ARGS
      PutS("TFU_ARGS - the job description cannot be encoded")
    Case #V3D_ERR_TFU_BUSY
      PutS("TFU_BUSY - the unit was busy before submission")
    Case #V3D_ERR_TFU_TIMEOUT
      PutS("TFU_TIMEOUT - CVTCT never moved")
    Case #V3D_ERR_TFU_FAIL
      PutS("TFU_FAIL - HUB_INT_STS.TFUF. The unit said no.")
    Default
      PutS("code ")
      PutDec(e)
  EndSelect
EndProcedure

Procedure PutQpuErr(e.i)
  Select e
    Case #V3DQ_OK
      PutS("OK")
    Case #V3DQ_ERR_ADD_OP
      PutS("ADD_OP - that ADD operation is not encoded")
    Case #V3DQ_ERR_SIG
      PutS("SIG - no 4.2 code for that signal combination")
    Case #V3DQ_ERR_RANGE
      PutS("RANGE - a waddr, mux or raddr is out of its field")
    Case #V3DQ_ERR_FULL
      PutS("FULL - the program buffer has no room")
    Case #V3DQ_ERR_NOBUF
      PutS("NOBUF - V3dQpuProgramBegin() was never called")
    Case #V3DQ_ERR_HAZARD
      PutS("HAZARD - a p37 restriction, rule ")
      PutDec(V3dQpuHazardName())
    Case #V3DQ_ERR_VPM_DEST
      PutS("VPM_DEST - a magic destination on a VPM load")
    Case #V3DQ_ERR_PACK
      PutS("PACK - an output pack this operation cannot take")
    Case #V3DQ_ERR_UNPACK
      PutS("UNPACK - an input unpack this operation cannot take")
    Default
      PutS("code ")
      PutDec(e)
  EndSelect
EndProcedure

Procedure DumpBytes(base.i, len.i)
  Define i.i
  i = 0
  While i < len
    If (i % 16) = 0
      PutS("  ")
      PutHex(base + i, 8)
      PutS(":")
    EndIf
    PutS(" ")
    PutHex(PeekA(base + i), 2)
    i = i + 1
    If (i % 16) = 0
      PutNl()
    EndIf
  Wend
  If (len % 16) <> 0
    PutNl()
  EndIf
EndProcedure

Procedure DumpProgram(base.i, count.i)
  Define i.i
  i = 0
  While i < count
    PutS("  Q ")
    PutDec(i)
    PutS(" ")
    PutHex(PeekN(base + (i * 8) + 4), 8)
    PutS(" ")
    PutHex(PeekN(base + (i * 8)), 8)
    PutNl()
    i = i + 1
  Wend
EndProcedure

; ======================================================================
;  THE THREE SHADERS
; ======================================================================

; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
;  THE COORDINATE SHADER. Eight values in, eight values out.
;
;  It is pi4V3dTri's coordinate shader with the loop bound raised from
;  six to eight. Inputs 0..5 are Xc Yc Zc Wc Xs Ys; inputs 6,7 are U,V
;  (the coord-phase VPM input offsets for attributes 8 and 9 - see
;  BuildRecords). Outputs 0..5 are the shaded-vertex position, outputs
;  6,7 are the two VARYINGS (varyings_vpm_offset = 6 for the coord
;  shader, v3d_nir_lower_io.c:414-430). in[k] -> out[k], a straight
;  copy of eight values.
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
Procedure.i BuildCoordShader()
  Define r.i
  Define k.i

  r = V3dQpuProgramBeginSeg(#TEX_CODE_CS, #TEX_CODE_SLOT, 1)
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf

  ; rf0..rf7 = the constants 0..7, the LDVPM offsets.
  k = 0
  While k < 8
    r = V3dQpuNopSig(#V3DQ_SIG_LDUNIFRF, k, 0)
    If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
    k = k + 1
  Wend

  ; rf8..rf15 = VPM input 0..7. (in[6]=U, in[7]=V in the coord phase.)
  k = 0
  While k < 8
    r = V3dQpuLdvpm(#V3DQ_A_LDVPMV_IN, 8 + k, #V3DQ_MUX_A, k)
    If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
    k = k + 1
  Wend

  ; VPM output 0..5 = position (rf8..rf13).
  k = 0
  While k < 6
    r = V3dQpuStvpm(#V3DQ_A_STVPMV, #V3DQ_MUX_A, #V3DQ_MUX_B, k, 8 + k)
    If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
    k = k + 1
  Wend

  ; VPM output 6,7 = the two varyings.
  If #TEX_FS_MODE = #TEX_MODE_DIRECT
    ; DIRECT DATA-PATH TEST: varying0 = Xc (in[0]), varying1 = Yc (in[1]) -
    ; a known-good float that varies per vertex, bypassing the U,V
    ; attribute plumbing entirely.
    r = V3dQpuStvpm(#V3DQ_A_STVPMV, #V3DQ_MUX_A, #V3DQ_MUX_B, 6, 8)
    If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
    r = V3dQpuStvpm(#V3DQ_A_STVPMV, #V3DQ_MUX_A, #V3DQ_MUX_B, 7, 9)
    If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
  Else
    ; NORMAL: varying0 = U (in[6]), varying1 = V (in[7]).
    r = V3dQpuStvpm(#V3DQ_A_STVPMV, #V3DQ_MUX_A, #V3DQ_MUX_B, 6, 14)
    If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
    r = V3dQpuStvpm(#V3DQ_A_STVPMV, #V3DQ_MUX_A, #V3DQ_MUX_B, 7, 15)
    If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
  EndIf

  r = V3dQpuAdd0(#V3DQ_A_VPMWT, #V3DQ_WADDR_NOP, 1)
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
  r = V3dQpuProgramEndThrsw()
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
  ProcedureReturn V3dQpuProgramEnd()
EndProcedure

; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
;  THE VERTEX SHADER. Six values out of ten in.
;
;  Reads VPM input 4..9 - Xs Ys Zs 1/Wc U V - and writes VPM output
;  0..5. Outputs 0..3 are the non-coord shaded vertex (Xs Ys Zs 1/Wc),
;  outputs 4,5 are the two VARYINGS (varyings_vpm_offset = 4 for the
;  vertex shader). out[k] = in[4+k], k = 0..5. pi4V3dTri's vertex
;  shader with the input offset base kept at 4 and the count raised
;  from four to six.
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
Procedure.i BuildVertexShader()
  Define r.i
  Define k.i

  r = V3dQpuProgramBeginSeg(#TEX_CODE_VS, #TEX_CODE_SLOT, 1)
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf

  ; rf0..rf9 = the constants 0..9. rf[4+k] holds the input offset 4+k
  ; and rf[k] holds the output slot index k.
  k = 0
  While k < 10
    r = V3dQpuNopSig(#V3DQ_SIG_LDUNIFRF, k, 0)
    If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
    k = k + 1
  Wend

  ; rf10..rf13 = VPM input 4..7 (Xs Ys Zs 1/Wc), the shaded position.
  k = 0
  While k < 4
    r = V3dQpuLdvpm(#V3DQ_A_LDVPMV_IN, 10 + k, #V3DQ_MUX_A, 4 + k)
    If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
    k = k + 1
  Wend

  ; rf14,rf15 = the two varying sources.
  If #TEX_FS_MODE = #TEX_MODE_DIRECT
    ; DIRECT DATA-PATH TEST: varying0 = Xc (in[0]), varying1 = Yc (in[1]).
    ; Offsets 0,1 come from rf0,rf1. Bypasses the U,V attribute plumbing.
    r = V3dQpuLdvpm(#V3DQ_A_LDVPMV_IN, 14, #V3DQ_MUX_A, 0)
    If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
    r = V3dQpuLdvpm(#V3DQ_A_LDVPMV_IN, 15, #V3DQ_MUX_A, 1)
    If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
  Else
    ; NORMAL: varying0 = U (in[8]), varying1 = V (in[9]).
    r = V3dQpuLdvpm(#V3DQ_A_LDVPMV_IN, 14, #V3DQ_MUX_A, 8)
    If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
    r = V3dQpuLdvpm(#V3DQ_A_LDVPMV_IN, 15, #V3DQ_MUX_A, 9)
    If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
  EndIf

  ; VPM output 0..5 = rf10..rf15 (position at 0..3, varyings at 4,5).
  k = 0
  While k < 6
    r = V3dQpuStvpm(#V3DQ_A_STVPMV, #V3DQ_MUX_A, #V3DQ_MUX_B, k, 10 + k)
    If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
    k = k + 1
  Wend

  r = V3dQpuAdd0(#V3DQ_A_VPMWT, #V3DQ_WADDR_NOP, 1)
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
  r = V3dQpuProgramEndThrsw()
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
  ProcedureReturn V3dQpuProgramEnd()
EndProcedure

; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
;  THE TEXTURED FRAGMENT SHADER (#TEX_FS_SOLID = 0). See the header.
;
;  Uniform stream, in program order: P0 (WRTMUC), P1 (WRTMUC), then the
;  TLB config word (pulled by the TLBU write). No LDUNIFRF at all - the
;  colour is the sampled texel.
;
;  Register use: rf10/rf11 the two varying interpolation values,
;  rf12/rf13 the S and T coordinates, rf0..rf3 the four returned texel
;  channels R,G,B,A. r5 is the LDVARY C coefficient, read one cycle
;  after the filler nop.
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
Procedure.i BuildTexturedFragmentShader()
  Define r.i

  r = V3dQpuProgramBeginSeg(#TEX_CODE_FS, #TEX_CODE_SLOT, 0)
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf

  ; --- TMU config P0, P1 via WRTMUC, one uniform each ---
  r = V3dQpuNopSig(#V3DQ_SIG_WRTMUC, 0, 0)
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
  r = V3dQpuNopSig(#V3DQ_SIG_WRTMUC, 0, 0)
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf

  ; --- varying 0 (U -> S). LDVARY writes rf10, loads r5 = C delayed ---
  r = V3dQpuNopSig(#V3DQ_SIG_LDVARY, 10, 0)
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
  r = V3dQpuNop()                         ; r5 delay slot
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
  r = V3dQpuAdd2(#V3DQ_A_FADD, 12, 0, #V3DQ_MUX_A, #V3DQ_MUX_R5, 10, 0)
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf

  ; --- varying 1 (V -> T) ---
  r = V3dQpuNopSig(#V3DQ_SIG_LDVARY, 11, 0)
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
  r = V3dQpuNop()                         ; r5 delay slot
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
  r = V3dQpuAdd2(#V3DQ_A_FADD, 13, 0, #V3DQ_MUX_A, #V3DQ_MUX_R5, 11, 0)
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf

  ; --- coordinate writes: T then S. Mov-via-OR in the ADD half, the
  ;     way Mesa writes TMU coordinates (vir_MOV = OR src,src). Writing
  ;     TMUS FIRES the lookup, so it is last. ---
  r = V3dQpuAdd2(#V3DQ_A_OR, #V3DQ_WADDR_TMUT, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_A, #V3DQ_MUX_A, 13, 0)
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
  r = V3dQpuAdd2(#V3DQ_A_OR, #V3DQ_WADDR_TMUS, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_A, #V3DQ_MUX_A, 12, 0)
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf

  ; --- THE THREAD SWITCH THAT DELIVERS THE TMU RESULT. On a threaded
  ;     fragment shader (fourWay = 1, as here and in pi4V3dTri) the
  ;     texel is returned to the thread only ACROSS a thread switch:
  ;     ntq_flush_tmu() emits vir_emit_thrsw() before the LDTMUs, and
  ;     vir_emit_thrsw()'s comment is "Always thread switch after each
  ;     texture operation" (nir_to_vir.c:266-271, :159). Without it the
  ;     LDTMUs stall forever and the render never completes - which is
  ;     exactly the RENDER_TIMEOUT this shader first produced. A THRSW
  ;     has two delay slots (qpu_schedule.c:2075), so two nops fill them
  ;     and the first LDTMU lands after the switch. This is a regular
  ;     thread switch, NOT the last-THRSW marker; the marker pair is
  ;     still emitted by V3dQpuLastThrsw() below. ---
  r = V3dQpuNopSig(#V3DQ_SIG_THRSW, 0, 0)
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
  r = V3dQpuNop()
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
  r = V3dQpuNop()
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf

  ; --- read the four texel channels R,G,B,A into rf0..rf3 ---
  r = V3dQpuNopSig(#V3DQ_SIG_LDTMU, 0, 0)
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
  r = V3dQpuNopSig(#V3DQ_SIG_LDTMU, 1, 0)
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
  r = V3dQpuNopSig(#V3DQ_SIG_LDTMU, 2, 0)
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
  r = V3dQpuNopSig(#V3DQ_SIG_LDTMU, 3, 0)
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf

  ; --- the last-THRSW pair and its two delay slots ---
  r = V3dQpuLastThrsw()
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf

  ; --- the TLB colour write, byte-for-byte pi4V3dTri's: TLBU carries
  ;     the config word from the uniform stream, TLB the second half ---
  r = V3dQpuVfpack(#V3DQ_WADDR_TLBU, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_A, #V3DQ_MUX_B, 0, 1)
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
  r = V3dQpuVfpack(#V3DQ_WADDR_TLB, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_A, #V3DQ_MUX_B, 2, 3)
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf

  r = V3dQpuProgramEndThrsw()
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
  ProcedureReturn V3dQpuProgramEnd()
EndProcedure

; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
;  THE SOLID FRAGMENT SHADER (#TEX_FS_MODE = 1) - the bisection build.
;
;  Reads and DISCARDS the two varyings with the SAME LDVARY + r5 + FADD
;  sequence as the textured shader, so the varying path is exercised
;  end to end. Then NO TMU work: it loads four colour components from
;  the uniform stream and writes them to the TLB the way pi4V3dTri's
;  flat shader does. If this renders, the render CL and the varying
;  setup are good and the hang is in the TMU path alone.
;
;  Uniform stream, in program order: R, G, B, A (four LDUNIFRF), then
;  the TLB config word (the TLBU write). No WRTMUC, no P0/P1.
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
Procedure.i BuildSolidFragmentShader()
  Define r.i

  r = V3dQpuProgramBeginSeg(#TEX_CODE_FS, #TEX_CODE_SLOT, 0)
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf

  ; --- varying 0, read and discarded ---
  r = V3dQpuNopSig(#V3DQ_SIG_LDVARY, 10, 0)
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
  r = V3dQpuNop()
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
  r = V3dQpuAdd2(#V3DQ_A_FADD, 12, 0, #V3DQ_MUX_A, #V3DQ_MUX_R5, 10, 0)
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf

  ; --- varying 1, read and discarded ---
  r = V3dQpuNopSig(#V3DQ_SIG_LDVARY, 11, 0)
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
  r = V3dQpuNop()
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
  r = V3dQpuAdd2(#V3DQ_A_FADD, 13, 0, #V3DQ_MUX_A, #V3DQ_MUX_R5, 11, 0)
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf

  ; --- rf0..rf3 = the four solid colour components from uniforms ---
  r = V3dQpuNopSig(#V3DQ_SIG_LDUNIFRF, 0, 0)
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
  r = V3dQpuNopSig(#V3DQ_SIG_LDUNIFRF, 1, 0)
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
  r = V3dQpuNopSig(#V3DQ_SIG_LDUNIFRF, 2, 0)
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
  r = V3dQpuNopSig(#V3DQ_SIG_LDUNIFRF, 3, 0)
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf

  r = V3dQpuLastThrsw()
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf

  r = V3dQpuVfpack(#V3DQ_WADDR_TLBU, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_A, #V3DQ_MUX_B, 0, 1)
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
  r = V3dQpuVfpack(#V3DQ_WADDR_TLB, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_A, #V3DQ_MUX_B, 2, 3)
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf

  r = V3dQpuProgramEndThrsw()
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
  ProcedureReturn V3dQpuProgramEnd()
EndProcedure

; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
;  THE U-RAMP FRAGMENT SHADER (#TEX_FS_MODE = 2) - the varying probe.
;
;  Reads varying 0 (U) with the SAME LDVARY + r5 + FADD sequence as the
;  textured shader (rf12 = U), reads and discards varying 1 (V) so the
;  varying FIFO is drained exactly as in the textured build, then writes
;  U to ALL FOUR channels: VFPACK(U,U) -> TLBU, VFPACK(U,U) -> TLB. The
;  framebuffer pixel becomes (U,U,U,U) as unorm8, so each byte is
;  round(U*255). NO TMU. The result makes the interpolated U directly
;  visible and machine-readable.
;
;  Uniform stream: the TLB config word only (pulled by the TLBU write).
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
Procedure.i BuildRampFragmentShader()
  Define r.i

  r = V3dQpuProgramBeginSeg(#TEX_CODE_FS, #TEX_CODE_SLOT, 0)
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf

  ; --- varying 0 (U) -> rf12 ---
  r = V3dQpuNopSig(#V3DQ_SIG_LDVARY, 10, 0)
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
  r = V3dQpuNop()
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
  r = V3dQpuAdd2(#V3DQ_A_FADD, 12, 0, #V3DQ_MUX_A, #V3DQ_MUX_R5, 10, 0)
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf

  ; --- varying 1 (V) read and discarded ---
  r = V3dQpuNopSig(#V3DQ_SIG_LDVARY, 11, 0)
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
  r = V3dQpuNop()
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
  r = V3dQpuAdd2(#V3DQ_A_FADD, 13, 0, #V3DQ_MUX_A, #V3DQ_MUX_R5, 11, 0)
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf

  r = V3dQpuLastThrsw()
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf

  ; --- write U to all four channels: pack(U,U) twice ---
  r = V3dQpuVfpack(#V3DQ_WADDR_TLBU, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_A, #V3DQ_MUX_A, 12, 0)
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
  r = V3dQpuVfpack(#V3DQ_WADDR_TLB, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_A, #V3DQ_MUX_A, 12, 0)
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf

  r = V3dQpuProgramEndThrsw()
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
  ProcedureReturn V3dQpuProgramEnd()
EndProcedure

; The dispatcher the rest of the program calls. Selected at compile time.
; DIRECT uses the same U-ramp fragment shader as RAMP; only the geometry
; shaders differ (they source the varyings from Xc,Yc).
Procedure.i BuildFragmentShader()
  If #TEX_FS_MODE = #TEX_MODE_RAMP Or #TEX_FS_MODE = #TEX_MODE_DIRECT
    ProcedureReturn BuildRampFragmentShader()
  EndIf
  If #TEX_FS_MODE = #TEX_MODE_SOLID
    ProcedureReturn BuildSolidFragmentShader()
  EndIf
  ProcedureReturn BuildTexturedFragmentShader()
EndProcedure

; ======================================================================
;  THE DATA
; ======================================================================

; One vertex: ten 32-bit values in attribute order -
; Xc Yc Zc Wc Xs Ys Zs 1/Wc U V. Stride 40.
Procedure PutVertex(n.i, xc.i, yc.i, xs.i, ys.i, u.i, v.i)
  Define b.i
  b = #TEX_VERTS + (n * 40)
  PokeN(b +  0, xc)
  PokeN(b +  4, yc)
  PokeN(b +  8, #TEX_F_ZERO)   ; Zc
  PokeN(b + 12, #TEX_F_ONE)    ; Wc
  PokeN(b + 16, xs)            ; Xs, an INTEGER in 1/256 pixel
  PokeN(b + 20, ys)            ; Ys
  PokeN(b + 24, #TEX_F_ZERO)   ; Zs
  PokeN(b + 28, #TEX_F_ONE)    ; 1/Wc
  PokeN(b + 32, u)             ; U, varying 0
  PokeN(b + 36, v)             ; V, varying 1
EndProcedure

Procedure BuildVerts()
  PutVertex(0, #TEX_F_M75, #TEX_F_M75, (#TEX_V0X - #TEX_CX) * 256, (#TEX_V0Y - #TEX_CY) * 256, #TEX_F_ZERO, #TEX_F_ZERO)
  PutVertex(1, #TEX_F_P75, #TEX_F_M75, (#TEX_V1X - #TEX_CX) * 256, (#TEX_V1Y - #TEX_CY) * 256, #TEX_F_ONE,  #TEX_F_ZERO)
  PutVertex(2, #TEX_F_M75, #TEX_F_P75, (#TEX_V2X - #TEX_CX) * 256, (#TEX_V2Y - #TEX_CY) * 256, #TEX_F_ZERO, #TEX_F_ONE)

  PokeN(#TEX_DEFAULTS +  0, #TEX_F_ZERO)
  PokeN(#TEX_DEFAULTS +  4, #TEX_F_ZERO)
  PokeN(#TEX_DEFAULTS +  8, #TEX_F_ZERO)
  PokeN(#TEX_DEFAULTS + 12, #TEX_F_ONE)
EndProcedure

Procedure BuildUniforms()
  Define k.i
  ; Coordinate shader: eight LDVPM offsets, constants 0..7.
  k = 0
  While k < 8
    PokeN(#TEX_UNIF_CS + (k * 4), k)
    k = k + 1
  Wend
  ; Vertex shader: constants 0..9.
  k = 0
  While k < 10
    PokeN(#TEX_UNIF_VS + (k * 4), k)
    k = k + 1
  Wend
  If #TEX_FS_MODE = #TEX_MODE_SOLID
    ; Solid build: four colour components, then the TLB config word, in
    ; the order the solid shader touches the stream (four LDUNIFRF, then
    ; the TLBU write). No P0/P1.
    PokeN(#TEX_UNIF_FS +  0, #TEX_SF_R)
    PokeN(#TEX_UNIF_FS +  4, #TEX_SF_G)
    PokeN(#TEX_UNIF_FS +  8, #TEX_SF_B)
    PokeN(#TEX_UNIF_FS + 12, #TEX_SF_A)
    PokeN(#TEX_UNIF_FS + 16, #TEX_TLB_CONF)
  ElseIf #TEX_FS_MODE = #TEX_MODE_RAMP Or #TEX_FS_MODE = #TEX_MODE_DIRECT
    ; U-ramp / direct build: only the TLB config word (pulled by the
    ; TLBU write). No colour uniforms, no P0/P1 - the colour is varying 0.
    PokeN(#TEX_UNIF_FS +  0, #TEX_TLB_CONF)
  Else
    ; Textured build: P0, P1, then the TLB config word, in the order the
    ; shader touches the stream (two WRTMUC, then the TLBU write).
    ;   P0 = texture state address | return-words mask ($F, four words).
    ;   P1 = sampler state address | output-type-32-bit (bit 0).
    PokeN(#TEX_UNIF_FS +  0, #TEX_TEXSTATE | $F)
    PokeN(#TEX_UNIF_FS +  4, #TEX_SAMPSTATE | 1)
    PokeN(#TEX_UNIF_FS +  8, #TEX_TLB_CONF)
  EndIf
EndProcedure

; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
;  BuildTexSrc - the 4x4 raster checkerboard, RGBA8. Columns 0,1 red,
;  columns 2,3 blue. Texel (x,y) at raster offset (y*4 + x)*4.
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
Procedure BuildTexSrc()
  Define x.i
  Define y.i
  Define off.i
  Define c.i
  y = 0
  While y < #TEX_TH
    x = 0
    While x < #TEX_TW
      off = ((y * #TEX_TW) + x) * 4
      If x < 2
        c = #TEX_RED
      Else
        c = #TEX_BLUE
      EndIf
      PokeN(#TEX_TEXSRC + off, c)
      x = x + 1
    Wend
    y = y + 1
  Wend
EndProcedure

; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
;  BuildTexState - the TEXTURE_SHADER_STATE (24 bytes) and the
;  SAMPLER_STATE (24 bytes), both packed by hand from v3d_packet.xml.
;
;  TEXTURE_SHADER_STATE, max_ver 42 (:1493-1532), by bit offset:
;    word0 bits   0.. 31  Texture base pointer (64-byte aligned; the
;                         low 6 bits hold the flip/sRGB flags, all 0).
;    word1 bits  32.. 57  Array Stride/64 = 0 (no array)
;          bits  58.. 71  Image Width  = 4  (low 6 bits -> word1<<26)
;    word2 bits  64.. 71  Image Width high 8 bits = 0
;          bits  72.. 85  Image Height = 4  (-> word2<<8)
;          bits  86.. 99  Image Depth  = 1  (low 10 bits -> word2<<22)
;    word3 bits  96.. 99  Image Depth high 4 bits = 0
;          bits 100..106  Texture type = RGBA8 = 4        (<<4)
;          bit  107       Extended = 0
;          bits 108..110  Swizzle R = Red   (2)           (<<12)
;          bits 111..113  Swizzle G = Green (3)           (<<15)
;          bits 114..116  Swizzle B = Blue  (4)           (<<18)
;          bits 117..119  Swizzle A = Alpha (5)           (<<21)
;          bits 120..127  Max/Base Level = 0
;    word4/word5           UB_PAD, XOR, strictly-UIF, pad - all 0
;      (NOT UIF: a 4x4 RGBA8 texture is LINEARTILE - level_width <=
;       utile_w picks it, v3d_resource.c:647-652 - so every UIF field
;       stays clear.)
;
;  SAMPLER_STATE (:1584-1618):
;    word0 bit 0  Mag filter Nearest = 1
;          bit 1  Min filter Nearest = 1
;          bit 7  sRGB Disable       = 1
;          (mip nearest 0, LODs 0)
;    word1 bits 48..50 Wrap S = CLAMP (1)  (-> word1<<16)
;          bits 51..53 Wrap T = CLAMP (1)  (-> word1<<19)
;    word2..word5  border colour 0
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
Procedure BuildTexState()
  ; Zero both records first (the pad and every unnamed flag).
  Define i.i
  i = 0
  While i < 8
    PokeN(#TEX_TEXSTATE  + (i * 4), 0)
    PokeN(#TEX_SAMPSTATE + (i * 4), 0)
    i = i + 1
  Wend

  ; TEXTURE_SHADER_STATE.
  PokeN(#TEX_TEXSTATE +  0, #TEX_TEX)
  PokeN(#TEX_TEXSTATE +  4, (4 << 26))
  PokeN(#TEX_TEXSTATE +  8, (4 << 8) | (1 << 22))
  PokeN(#TEX_TEXSTATE + 12, (4 << 4) | (2 << 12) | (3 << 15) | (4 << 18) | (5 << 21))

  ; SAMPLER_STATE.
  PokeN(#TEX_SAMPSTATE +  0, 1 | 2 | $80)
  PokeN(#TEX_SAMPSTATE +  4, (1 << 16) | (1 << 19))
EndProcedure

; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
;  THE SHADER STATE RECORD AND TEN ATTRIBUTE RECORDS.
;
;  Ten attributes, one 32-bit value each, stride 40. cs (coordinate
;  phase) reads attributes 0-5 and 8-9 (position + U,V); attributes 6-7
;  (Zs, 1/Wc) are vertex-phase only. vs reads all ten. So the coord
;  shader's VPM input has U,V at offsets 6,7 and the vertex shader's at
;  8,9 - which is why BuildCoordShader reads 6,7 and BuildVertexShader
;  reads 8,9.
;
;  numVaryingsFs = 2. Attributes 4,5 (Xs,Ys) are signed ints, as in
;  pi4V3dTri.
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
Procedure.i BuildRecords()
  Define r.i
  Define k.i
  Define cs.i

  r = V3dShaderRecordBegin(#TEX_SHREC, 10)
  If r <> #V3D_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf

  V3dShaderRecordFlags(1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 2)
  ; vsOutSeg = 2 WAS THE VARYING BUG. Segments are SHARED, so the OUTPUT
  ; field carries MAX(output,input) in 8-value sectors (v3dx_draw.c:640-660,
  ; vir.c:846-857). Vertex INPUT = 10 attribute values = 2 sectors, output =
  ; 6 = 1, so MAX = 2. At 1 the shared segment held only 8 values, so vertex
  ; VPM inputs 8,9 (U,V) overflowed and were delivered as 0 - the constant
  ; varying. Coord MAX(8,8)=1 sector. VCM stays 4 (16 KiB VPM, half 16, /2-1).
  V3dShaderRecordVpm(1, 0, 1, 1, 2, 0, 1, 1)
  V3dShaderRecordDefaults(#TEX_DEFAULTS)
  V3dShaderRecordFragment(#TEX_CODE_FS, #TEX_UNIF_FS, 1, 0, 1)
  V3dShaderRecordVertex(#TEX_CODE_VS, #TEX_UNIF_VS, 1, 1, 1)
  V3dShaderRecordCoord(#TEX_CODE_CS, #TEX_UNIF_CS, 1, 1, 1)

  k = 0
  While k < 10
    cs = 1
    If k = 6 Or k = 7
      cs = 0
    EndIf
    V3dAttrRecord(k, #TEX_VERTS + (k * 4), 40, $FFFFFF, cs, 1)
    k = k + 1
  Wend
  V3dAttrRecordType(4, 1, #V3D_ATTR_INT, 1, 0, 1, 0)
  V3dAttrRecordType(5, 1, #V3D_ATTR_INT, 1, 0, 1, 0)

  If V3dShaderRecordOk() = 0
    ProcedureReturn #V3D_ERR_CL_ARGS
  EndIf
  ProcedureReturn #V3D_OK
EndProcedure

; ======================================================================
;  VERIFICATION
; ======================================================================

Global nRed.i    = 0
Global nBlue.i   = 0
Global nSolid.i  = 0
Global nClear.i  = 0
Global nPoison.i = 0
Global nOther.i  = 0
Global firstOther.i = -1
Global firstOtherVal.i = 0
Global redMinX.i  = 9999
Global redMaxX.i  = -1
Global blueMinX.i = 9999
Global blueMaxX.i = -1
Global redMinY.i  = 9999
Global redMaxY.i  = -1
Global blueMinY.i = 9999
Global blueMaxY.i = -1
Global guardTouched.i = 0

; U-ramp analysis: over drawn (non-clear, non-poison) pixels, the low
; byte is round(U*255). Track its range and the x where the min and max
; occur, so a gradient (min at small x, max at large x) is visible.
Global grayMin.i  = 999
Global grayMax.i  = -1
Global grayMinX.i = -1
Global grayMaxX.i = -1
Global nGray.i    = 0

Procedure.i PixelAt(x.i, y.i)
  ProcedureReturn PeekN(#TEX_TARGET + (y * #TEX_STRIDE) + (x * 4))
EndProcedure

Procedure Verify()
  Define x.i
  Define y.i
  Define v.i
  Define g.i

  y = 0
  While y < #TEX_H
    x = 0
    While x < #TEX_W
      v = PixelAt(x, y)
      If v = #TEX_RED
        nRed = nRed + 1
        If x < redMinX : redMinX = x : EndIf
        If x > redMaxX : redMaxX = x : EndIf
        If y < redMinY : redMinY = y : EndIf
        If y > redMaxY : redMaxY = y : EndIf
      ElseIf v = #TEX_BLUE
        nBlue = nBlue + 1
        If x < blueMinX : blueMinX = x : EndIf
        If x > blueMaxX : blueMaxX = x : EndIf
        If y < blueMinY : blueMinY = y : EndIf
        If y > blueMaxY : blueMaxY = y : EndIf
      ElseIf v = #TEX_SOLID
        nSolid = nSolid + 1
      ElseIf v = #TEX_CLEAR
        nClear = nClear + 1
      ElseIf v = #TEX_POISON
        nPoison = nPoison + 1
      Else
        nOther = nOther + 1
        If firstOther < 0
          firstOther = (y * #TEX_W) + x
          firstOtherVal = v
        EndIf
        ; A drawn pixel that is not one of the named colours. In the
        ; U-ramp build every triangle pixel lands here; its low byte is
        ; round(U*255). Track the range and where it occurs.
        g = v & $FF
        nGray = nGray + 1
        If g < grayMin
          grayMin = g
          grayMinX = x
        EndIf
        If g > grayMax
          grayMax = g
          grayMaxX = x
        EndIf
      EndIf
      x = x + 1
    Wend
    y = y + 1
  Wend
EndProcedure

Procedure VerifyGuard()
  Define i.i
  Define n.i
  i = 0
  n = #TEX_GUARD_BYTES / 4
  While i < n
    If PeekN(#TEX_GUARD + (i * 4)) <> #TEX_POISON
      guardTouched = guardTouched + 1
    EndIf
    i = i + 1
  Wend
EndProcedure

; ======================================================================
;  EXPLICIT VARYING-FLAG PACKETS
;
;  THE ZERO_ALL SHORTCUT WAS THE VARYING BUG. On silicon, emitting
;  Zero All Non-perspective Flags (code 99) left the fragment shader's
;  two varyings PERSPECTIVE, while the fragment shader reads them with
;  the NO-PERSPECTIVE arithmetic (vary + r5). The mismatch delivered the
;  provoking-vertex value - every fragment's U came back as 0, the value
;  at vertices 0 and 2 - which read as flat shading.
;
;  The flags packet and the fragment-shader arithmetic MUST AGREE. These
;  emit the explicit packets so they do:
;
;    Flat Shade Flags     (v3d_packet.xml code 98)  - all bits 0: no
;                         varying is flat, both are smooth.
;    Non-perspective Flags (code 100)               - bits for varyings
;                         0 and 1 SET: both are no-perspective, matching
;                         the fragment shader. For an affine (Wc=1) quad
;                         screen-linear interpolation is the correct
;                         interpolation, so this is exact.
;
;  Packet layout (both), from the field offsets:
;    byte 0  Varying offset V0 (bits 0-3) | action lower (4-5) |
;            action higher (6-7). Offset 0, both actions ZEROED (=1) so
;            every varying outside the explicit window is cleared: $50.
;    bytes 1-3  the 24-bit flags for varyings 0..23, little-endian.
;
;  Emitted with v3d.pi4's low-level v3d_ClU8 into the open bin list, in
;  the same position the Zero All calls held.
; ======================================================================
Procedure EmitFlatShadeFlags(flags.i)
  v3d_ClU8(98)
  v3d_ClU8($50)
  v3d_ClU8(flags & $FF)
  v3d_ClU8((flags >> 8) & $FF)
  v3d_ClU8((flags >> 16) & $FF)
EndProcedure

Procedure EmitNonperspFlags(flags.i)
  v3d_ClU8(100)
  v3d_ClU8($50)
  v3d_ClU8(flags & $FF)
  v3d_ClU8((flags >> 8) & $FF)
  v3d_ClU8((flags >> 16) & $FF)
EndProcedure

; ======================================================================
;  MAIN
; ======================================================================

Procedure Main()
  Define r.i
  Define i.i
  Define n.i
  Define csBytes.i
  Define vsBytes.i
  Define fsBytes.i
  Define ok.i
  Define sx.i

  PutNl()
  PutS("=== Pi 4 V3D M1 - one TEXTURED triangle, TMU-sampled ===")
  PutNl()
  If #TEX_FS_MODE = #TEX_MODE_SOLID
    PutS("    FRAGMENT SHADER: SOLID bisection build (no TMU)")
  ElseIf #TEX_FS_MODE = #TEX_MODE_RAMP
    PutS("    FRAGMENT SHADER: U-RAMP build (varying U as grayscale, no TMU)")
  ElseIf #TEX_FS_MODE = #TEX_MODE_DIRECT
    PutS("    FRAGMENT SHADER: DIRECT-Xc RAMP (varyings = Xc,Yc, no attribute, no TMU)")
  Else
    PutS("    FRAGMENT SHADER: TEXTURED build (TMU sample)")
  EndIf
  PutNl()
  PutNl()

  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;  0. Stage 0.
  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  r = V3dInit()
  PutS("0   stage 0: ")
  PutErr(r)
  PutNl()
  RowHex("HUB_IDENT1", V3dIdent1())
  If r <> #V3D_OK
    PutS("verdict: STAGE0")
    PutNl()
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf
  PutNl()

  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;  1. THE THREE QPU PROGRAMS, BUILT AND PRINTED FIRST.
  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  PutS("1   the shaders")
  PutNl()

  r = BuildCoordShader()
  csBytes = V3dQpuProgramBytes()
  PutS("    coordinate shader: ")
  PutQpuErr(r)
  PutNl()
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK
    PutS("verdict: SHADER")
    PutNl()
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf
  RowDec("instructions", csBytes / 8)
  DumpProgram(#TEX_CODE_CS, csBytes / 8)

  r = BuildVertexShader()
  vsBytes = V3dQpuProgramBytes()
  PutS("    vertex shader: ")
  PutQpuErr(r)
  PutNl()
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK
    PutS("verdict: SHADER")
    PutNl()
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf
  RowDec("instructions", vsBytes / 8)
  DumpProgram(#TEX_CODE_VS, vsBytes / 8)

  r = BuildFragmentShader()
  fsBytes = V3dQpuProgramBytes()
  PutS("    fragment shader: ")
  PutQpuErr(r)
  PutNl()
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK
    PutS("verdict: SHADER")
    PutNl()
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf
  RowDec("instructions", fsBytes / 8)
  DumpProgram(#TEX_CODE_FS, fsBytes / 8)
  PutNl()

  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;  2. THE V3D MMU. Mapped BEFORE the TFU, which is a bus master and
  ;     reaches everything through the same page table.
  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  PutS("2   the V3D MMU: ")
  r = V3dMmuInit(#TEX_PT, #TEX_PT_BYTES, #TEX_ILLEGAL)
  PutErr(r)
  PutNl()
  If r <> #V3D_OK
    PutS("verdict: MMU")
    PutNl()
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf

  r = V3dMmuMap(#TEX_BCL, #TEX_BCL, #TEX_BCL_BYTES)
  If r = #V3D_OK
    r = V3dMmuMap(#TEX_TILELIST, #TEX_TILELIST, #TEX_TL_BYTES)
  EndIf
  If r = #V3D_OK
    r = V3dMmuMap(#TEX_RCL, #TEX_RCL, #TEX_RCL_BYTES)
  EndIf
  If r = #V3D_OK
    r = V3dMmuMap(#TEX_TSTATE, #TEX_TSTATE, #TEX_TSTATE_BYTES)
  EndIf
  If r = #V3D_OK
    r = V3dMmuMap(#TEX_SHREC, #TEX_SHREC, #TEX_SHREC_BYTES)
  EndIf
  If r = #V3D_OK
    r = V3dMmuMap(#TEX_VERTS, #TEX_VERTS, #TEX_VERTS_BYTES)
  EndIf
  If r = #V3D_OK
    r = V3dMmuMap(#TEX_UNIF_CS, #TEX_UNIF_CS, #TEX_UNIF_BYTES)
  EndIf
  If r = #V3D_OK
    r = V3dMmuMap(#TEX_CODE_CS, #TEX_CODE_CS, #TEX_CODE_BYTES)
  EndIf
  If r = #V3D_OK
    r = V3dMmuMap(#TEX_TARGET, #TEX_TARGET, #TEX_TARGET_BYTES)
  EndIf
  If r = #V3D_OK
    r = V3dMmuMap(#TEX_TEXSRC, #TEX_TEXSRC, #TEX_PAGE)
  EndIf
  If r = #V3D_OK
    r = V3dMmuMap(#TEX_TEX, #TEX_TEX, #TEX_TEX_BYTES)
  EndIf
  If r = #V3D_OK
    r = V3dMmuMap(#TEX_TEXSTATE, #TEX_TEXSTATE, #TEX_PAGE)
  EndIf
  If r = #V3D_OK
    r = V3dMmuMap(#TEX_TALLOC, #TEX_TALLOC, #TEX_TALLOC_BYTES)
  EndIf
  If r = #V3D_OK
    r = V3dMmuMap(#TEX_OVERFLOW, #TEX_OVERFLOW, #TEX_OVERFLOW_BYTES)
  EndIf
  If r <> #V3D_OK
    PutS("    mapping: ") : PutErr(r) : PutNl()
    PutS("verdict: MMU")
    PutNl()
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf
  RowDec("pages mapped", V3dMmuPagesMapped())
  RowHex("PTE for the texture", V3dMmuEntry(#TEX_TEX))
  RowHex("PTE for the guard page", V3dMmuEntry(#TEX_GUARD))
  PutNl()

  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;  3. THE TEXTURE. Build a raster checkerboard, TFU-tile it to the
  ;     LINEARTILE texture the TMU will sample. For a 4x4 image
  ;     LINEARTILE equals raster (one 64-byte microtile), so this is an
  ;     identity re-tile - it exercises the real path at the size where
  ;     its result is independently obvious.
  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  PutS("3   the texture")
  PutNl()
  ; Poison the tiled texture so a TFU that wrote nothing is visible.
  i = 0
  While i < (#TEX_TBYTES / 4)
    PokeN(#TEX_TEX + (i * 4), #TEX_POISON)
    i = i + 1
  Wend
  BuildTexSrc()
  PutS("    source 4x4 RGBA8 (red cols 0-1, blue cols 2-3):")
  PutNl()
  DumpBytes(#TEX_TEXSRC, #TEX_TBYTES)

  r = V3dTfuBegin(#TEX_TW, #TEX_TH, #V3D_TEXFMT_RGBA8)
  If r = #V3D_OK
    r = V3dTfuSourceRaster(#TEX_TEXSRC, #TEX_TW, #TEX_TBYTES)
  EndIf
  If r = #V3D_OK
    r = V3dTfuDest(#TEX_TEX, #V3D_TFU_OFMT_LINEARTILE, #TEX_TBYTES)
  EndIf
  If r = #V3D_OK
    r = V3dTfuSubmit()
  EndIf
  PutS("    TFU submit: ")
  PutErr(r)
  PutNl()
  If r <> #V3D_OK
    PutS("verdict: TFU")
    PutNl()
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf
  r = V3dTfuWait(#V3D_TFU_TIMEOUT_US)
  PutS("    TFU wait: ")
  PutErr(r)
  PutNl()
  If r <> #V3D_OK
    PutS("verdict: TFU")
    PutNl()
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf
  PutS("    tiled texture (LINEARTILE):")
  PutNl()
  DumpBytes(#TEX_TEX, #TEX_TBYTES)

  ; The texture and sampler state records.
  BuildTexState()
  PutS("    texture shader state (24 bytes):")
  PutNl()
  DumpBytes(#TEX_TEXSTATE, 24)
  PutS("    sampler state (24 bytes):")
  PutNl()
  DumpBytes(#TEX_SAMPSTATE, 24)
  PutNl()

  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;  4. THE FRAME GEOMETRY.
  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  r = V3dRenderBegin(#TEX_W, #TEX_H, #V3D_OFMT_RGBA8)
  PutS("4   the frame: ")
  PutErr(r)
  PutNl()
  If r <> #V3D_OK
    PutS("verdict: GEOMETRY")
    PutNl()
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf
  RowDec("tile alloc needed", V3dTileAllocNeeded())
  RowDec("tile alloc given", #TEX_TALLOC_BYTES)

  r = V3dRenderTarget(#TEX_TARGET, #TEX_TARGET_BYTES, #V3D_MEMFMT_RASTER, #TEX_STRIDE, 0)
  If r <> #V3D_OK
    PutS("    the render target: ") : PutErr(r) : PutNl()
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf
  V3dRenderClear(#TEX_CLEAR, #TEX_ZCLEAR, 0)
  r = V3dRenderPool(#TEX_TALLOC, #TEX_TALLOC_BYTES, #TEX_TSTATE, #TEX_TSTATE_BYTES)
  If r <> #V3D_OK
    PutS("    the pools: ") : PutErr(r) : PutNl()
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf
  r = V3dBinOverflow(#TEX_OVERFLOW, #TEX_OVERFLOW_BYTES)
  If r <> #V3D_OK
    PutS("    the overflow pool: ") : PutErr(r) : PutNl()
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf
  PutNl()

  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;  5. THE DATA, THE RECORDS, THE POISON.
  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  BuildVerts()
  BuildUniforms()

  i = 0
  n = #TEX_PAGE / 4
  While i < n
    PokeN(#TEX_SHREC + (i * 4), #TEX_POISON)
    i = i + 1
  Wend

  r = BuildRecords()
  PutS("5   the shader state record: ")
  PutErr(r)
  PutNl()
  If r <> #V3D_OK
    PutS("verdict: RECORD")
    PutNl()
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf
  RowHex("record", V3dShaderRecordAddr())
  RowDec("record + attrs, bytes", V3dShaderRecordBytes())
  DumpBytes(V3dShaderRecordAddr(), V3dShaderRecordBytes())
  PutS("    the three vertices, ten words each:")
  PutNl()
  DumpBytes(#TEX_VERTS, 120)
  PutNl()

  ; Poison the target and the guard page.
  i = 0
  n = #TEX_TARGET_BYTES / 4
  While i < n
    PokeN(#TEX_TARGET + (i * 4), #TEX_POISON)
    i = i + 1
  Wend
  i = 0
  n = #TEX_GUARD_BYTES / 4
  While i < n
    PokeN(#TEX_GUARD + (i * 4), #TEX_POISON)
    i = i + 1
  Wend
  i = 0
  n = 4096 / 4
  While i < n
    PokeN(#TEX_TALLOC + (i * 4), #TEX_POISON)
    PokeN(#TEX_TSTATE + (i * 4), #TEX_POISON)
    i = i + 1
  Wend

  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;  6. THE BIN LIST. Mesa's order, exactly as pi4V3dTri, EXCEPT the
  ;     varying flags: the two varyings are declared NO-PERSPECTIVE with
  ;     an explicit Non-perspective Flags packet so the flags agree with
  ;     the fragment shader's (vary + r5) arithmetic. numVaryingsFs=2 is
  ;     in the record (above). See EmitNonperspFlags for the argument.
  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  r = V3dBclBegin(#TEX_BCL, #TEX_BCL_BYTES)
  If r = #V3D_OK
    V3dClClipWindow(0, 0, #TEX_W, #TEX_H)
    V3dClCfgBits(V3dCfgBitsWord(1, 1, 0, 7))
    V3dClPointSize(#TEX_F_ONE)
    V3dClLineWidth(#TEX_F_ONE)
    V3dClClipperXyScaling(#TEX_F_8192, #TEX_F_8192)
    V3dClClipperZScaleOffset(#TEX_F_ONE, #TEX_F_ZERO)
    V3dClClipperZMinMax($BF800000, #TEX_F_ONE)
    V3dClViewportOffset((#TEX_CX * 256), 0, (#TEX_CY * 256), 0)
    V3dClColorWriteMasks(0)
    EmitFlatShadeFlags(0)          ; explicit: no varying is flat (smooth)
    EmitNonperspFlags($3)          ; explicit: varyings 0,1 no-perspective
    V3dClZeroAllCentroidFlags()
    V3dClOcclusionQueryCounter(0)
    V3dClSampleState($3F80, $F)
    V3dClVcmCacheSize(4, 4)
    V3dClGlShaderState(V3dShaderRecordAddr(), 10)
    V3dClVertexArrayPrims(#V3D_PRIM_TRIANGLES, 3, 0)
    r = V3dBclFinish()
  EndIf
  PutS("6   the bin list: ")
  PutErr(r)
  PutNl()
  If r <> #V3D_OK
    PutS("verdict: BCL")
    PutNl()
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf
  RowDec("bin list bytes", V3dBclBytes())
  DumpBytes(V3dBclStartAddr(), V3dBclBytes())
  PutNl()

  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;  7. THE RENDER LIST.
  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  r = V3dRclBuild(#TEX_TILELIST, #TEX_TL_BYTES, #TEX_RCL, #TEX_RCL_BYTES)
  PutS("7   the render list: ")
  PutErr(r)
  PutNl()
  If r <> #V3D_OK
    PutS("verdict: RCL")
    PutNl()
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf
  PutNl()

  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;  8. CACHE MAINTENANCE and the GPU caches. The shader record, verts,
  ;     uniforms, code, texture, and both state records are all reached
  ;     through the record and the library never sees their extents.
  ;     V3dInvalidateCaches() drops the TMU/L2T caches so the sample
  ;     reads the TFU's fresh output rather than a stale line.
  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  V3dCacheRange(#TEX_SHREC, V3dShaderRecordBytes())
  V3dCacheRange(#TEX_VERTS, 512)
  V3dCacheRange(#TEX_UNIF_CS, 256)
  V3dCacheRange(#TEX_CODE_CS, #TEX_CODE_SLOT * 3)
  V3dCacheRange(#TEX_TEX, #TEX_TBYTES)
  V3dCacheRange(#TEX_TEXSTATE, 512)
  V3dBarrier()
  V3dInvalidateCaches()

  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;  9. THE BIN JOB.
  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  r = V3dBinSubmit()
  PutS("8   bin submit: ")
  PutErr(r)
  PutNl()
  If r <> #V3D_OK
    PutS("verdict: BINSUBMIT")
    PutNl()
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf
  r = V3dBinWait(#TEX_WAIT_US)
  PutS("    bin wait: ")
  PutErr(r)
  PutNl()
  RowHex("CLE_BFC after", V3dBinBfcAfter())
  RowHex("CTL_INT_STS", V3dBinIntSts())
  RowHex("ERR_STAT", V3dBinErrStat())
  RowHex("MMU_VIO_ADDR", V3dBinVioAddr())
  If r <> #V3D_OK
    PutS("verdict: BIN")
    PutNl()
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf

  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;  10. THE RENDER JOB.
  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  r = V3dRenderSubmit()
  PutS("9   render submit: ")
  PutErr(r)
  PutNl()
  If r <> #V3D_OK
    PutS("verdict: RENDERSUBMIT")
    PutNl()
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf
  r = V3dRenderWait(#TEX_WAIT_US)
  PutS("    render wait: ")
  PutErr(r)
  PutNl()
  RowHex("CLE_RFC after", V3dRenderRfcAfter())
  RowHex("CTL_INT_STS", V3dRenderIntSts())
  RowHex("ERR_STAT", V3dRenderErrStat())
  RowHex("MMU_VIO_ADDR", V3dRenderVioAddr())
  PutNl()

  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;  11. THE PIXELS. This is the whole test.
  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Verify()
  VerifyGuard()

  PutS("10  the pixels")
  PutNl()
  RowDec("pixels total", #TEX_PIXELS)
  RowHex("red texel colour", #TEX_RED)
  RowDec("pixels red", nRed)
  RowHex("blue texel colour", #TEX_BLUE)
  RowDec("pixels blue", nBlue)
  RowHex("solid colour (bisect)", #TEX_SOLID)
  RowDec("pixels solid", nSolid)
  RowHex("clear colour", #TEX_CLEAR)
  RowDec("pixels clear colour", nClear)
  RowDec("pixels still poison", nPoison)
  RowDec("pixels some other value", nOther)
  RowDec("first other, pixel index", firstOther)
  RowHex("first other, value", firstOtherVal)
  RowDec("red   min x", redMinX)
  RowDec("red   max x", redMaxX)
  RowDec("blue  min x", blueMinX)
  RowDec("blue  max x", blueMaxX)
  RowDec("red   y range min", redMinY)
  RowDec("red   y range max", redMaxY)
  RowDec("blue  y range min", blueMinY)
  RowDec("blue  y range max", blueMaxY)
  RowDec("guard words touched", guardTouched)
  PutNl()

  ; A few named probes for the log.
  PutS("    probes (x,y) -> colour:")
  PutNl()
  RowHex("(16,20) expect red", PixelAt(16, 20))
  RowHex("(20,30) expect red", PixelAt(20, 30))
  RowHex("(40,12) expect blue", PixelAt(40, 12))
  RowHex("(44,14) expect blue", PixelAt(44, 14))
  PutNl()

  ; U-ramp analysis: the gradient of varying0 along a scan line, plus range.
  If #TEX_FS_MODE = #TEX_MODE_RAMP Or #TEX_FS_MODE = #TEX_MODE_DIRECT
    PutS("    varying0 across the triangle (drawn-pixel low byte):")
    PutNl()
    RowDec("gray pixels", nGray)
    RowDec("gray min (U8)", grayMin)
    RowDec("  at x", grayMinX)
    RowDec("gray max (U8)", grayMax)
    RowDec("  at x", grayMaxX)
    RowDec("gray spread max-min", grayMax - grayMin)
    PutS("    scan y=20, x=10..55 step 5, R-channel byte:")
    PutNl()
    sx = 10
    While sx <= 55
      PutS("      x=")
      PutDec(sx)
      PutS(" -> ")
      PutHex(PixelAt(sx, 20) & $FF, 2)
      PutS("  (full ")
      PutHex(PixelAt(sx, 20), 8)
      PutS(")")
      PutNl()
      sx = sx + 5
    Wend
    PutNl()
  EndIf

  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;  THE VERDICT.
  ;
  ;  Textured build: a pass needs BOTH texture colours present, EVERY
  ;  red pixel strictly left of EVERY blue pixel (the U varying
  ;  interpolated across X and the TMU split the texture), nothing
  ;  outside the known colours, no poison left, and the guard untouched.
  ;  The colour depends on X alone, so no Y convention is assumed.
  ;
  ;  Solid bisection build: a pass only means THE RENDER RAN - the
  ;  triangle area is the solid colour, no poison remains. It proves the
  ;  render CL, the varying-emitting coord/vertex shaders and the shader
  ;  record; it says nothing about the TMU.
  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ok = 0
  If #TEX_FS_MODE = #TEX_MODE_SOLID
    If nSolid > 0
      If nPoison = 0
        If guardTouched = 0
          ok = 1
        EndIf
      EndIf
    EndIf
    If ok = 1
      PutS("verdict: SOLID-OK - render ran, tile filled. TMU NOT tested; bug is in the TMU path.")
    Else
      PutS("verdict: SOLID-FAIL - render did not fill the tile. Bug is in the varying setup or the render CL, NOT the TMU.")
    EndIf
  ElseIf #TEX_FS_MODE = #TEX_MODE_RAMP Or #TEX_FS_MODE = #TEX_MODE_DIRECT
    ; varying0 interpolates iff the grey level spans a real range AND its
    ; maximum is to the RIGHT of its minimum (it grows with x). A spread
    ; under 8/255 is "flat". In DIRECT mode varying0 = Xc, which is
    ; negative on the left half and clamps to 0 there, so the gradient is
    ; on the right half - the max-right test still holds.
    If nGray > 0
      If (grayMax - grayMin) >= 8
        If grayMaxX > grayMinX
          ok = 1
        EndIf
      EndIf
    EndIf
    If ok = 1
      PutS("verdict: RAMP-OK - varying0 interpolates left-to-right. The interpolator works.")
    Else
      PutS("verdict: RAMP-FLAT - varying0 is (near) constant. It is NOT interpolating.")
    EndIf
  Else
    If nRed > 0
      If nBlue > 0
        If redMaxX < blueMinX
          If nPoison = 0
            If nOther = 0
              If guardTouched = 0
                ok = 1
              EndIf
            EndIf
          EndIf
        EndIf
      EndIf
    EndIf
    If ok = 1
      PutS("verdict: OK - TEXTURED TRIANGLE. red left of blue, TMU sampled.")
    Else
      PutS("verdict: NO TEXTURE")
    EndIf
  EndIf
  PutNl()

  ProcedureReturn nRed + nBlue + nSolid + nGray
EndProcedure
